+# Name utilities
+
+`normalizeName(value)` accepts a string, trims its ends and collapses consecutive whitespace to one space. Empty or whitespace-only strings normalize to an empty string. Nonstrings throw `TypeError`.
+
+```js
+import { normalizeName } from './src/index.js';
+normalizeName('  Ada   Lovelace ');
+```
+
+The example returns `Ada Lovelace`.
+
+Before changing normalization, read [the implementation](src/index.js) and [behavior tests](test/name.test.js). The tests exercise whitespace normalization and nonstring rejection. Run `npm test` from the repository root; the [package manifest](package.json) delegates to Node's test runner.

